# Job: dotnet framework — session rejection after the shutdown seal must not block the shared STREAM lane; host shutdown converges within its deadline

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Cap 3 h. Read `AGENTS.md` §2/§3/§4.1/§5, `framework/AGENTS.md`. Campaign rules: no mitigations (no new timeouts/retries/timers), one owner per rule, fewer rules, public API unchanged, regression test per fix (public API, deterministic), cross-language parity. Never modify `core/**`, `bindings/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/**`, `doc/site/**`, other languages, `framework/languages/dotnet/perf/**`, or `Runtime/Service/ZLinkManagedMeshNode.cs` / `MeshNodeShutdownSealTests.cs` (another job). Do not commit. dotnet env: `source framework/languages/dotnet/perf/scripts/dotnet-env.sh`; `/tmp/zlink-dotnet-gate.lock` for builds/tests, `/tmp/zlink-samples-gate.lock` for samples. Check `/proc/loadavg` < 10 and `pgrep -c lto1` == 0 before gates.

## Diagnosis (supervisor-verified; `doc/plan/c016-worklog/diag-perf-routemesh-timeouts-sigterm-summary.md` §B)
After the shutdown admission seal, `Runtime/Streams/ZLinkStreamSessionTable.cs:196-212` `RejectNewSession` sends the session-closing control with `SendFlags.None` (blocking, socket send timeout 1000 ms) inside the shared `_lane` of `Runtime/Backend/DotNet/Wrappers/ZLinkBackendStreamSocketWrapper.cs:126-133/351-360`; every other session's DONTWAIT closing/heartbeat waits behind it, the send is not bound to the host shutdown cancellation (`ZLinkDrainCoordinator.cs:493-496` passes the token to the executor but not here), so shutdown took 5.8 s at 64 connections and never finished at 512 (SIGKILL after 75 s; last step `stream_session_drain_failed → force_stop_begin TeardownFailed`). `ZLinkStreamSessionRuntime.cs:477-492` also turns ServerDrain `NotConnected` to a closed peer into `MarkTerminalFailed` and `ZLinkFrameworkDrainExecutor.cs:256-275` projects it as `TeardownFailed` without preserving the cause. Node (`stream-session-runtime.ts:1361-1377` closeForDrain, `managed-stream.ts:153-175` awaitable submit) and Java (`ZLinkStreamRuntime.java:1457-1474` sendAsync) use non-blocking submits — the .NET blocking NONE call inside the shared lane is the structural difference.
Spec: host relocation §14 (seal, accepted work, deadline, transport teardown — bounded teardown must converge; `ForceStopped/TeardownFailed` only after the budget), D-097/D-098.

## Task
1. Rejection/closing control sends use the same non-blocking submit path as other session controls (DONTWAIT/async completion) and observe the host shutdown cancellation; no per-call timeout added. One owner for "how a control is submitted".
2. A ServerDrain/closing send to an already-closed peer (`NotConnected`) is a completed teardown for that session, not a terminal failure; where a failure is real, the original exception/kind is preserved through `MarkTerminalFailed` → drain executor → `TeardownFailed` cause.
3. Regression (public API, unit project): host with N (e.g. 64) STREAM sessions where the seal rejects late sessions/controls → shutdown completes `Stopped/None` well inside the orderly deadline; a scaled variant (256+) as a contract test if runtime allows, otherwise justify. Assert the controls did not serialize on a blocking send (e.g. by timing bound derived from the deadline, not sleeps).
4. Gates: unit split (`--filter 'FullyQualifiedName!~CanonicalActorJoinIngressReplyTests'` + complement, `--blame-hang --blame-hang-timeout 10m`), SampleRegression, samples 7/7 under the locks. Then rerun the perf session-echo-only 64-connection SIGTERM repro from the diagnosis artifacts (`/dev/shm/zlink-perf-dotnet/diag-followup-20260906`, read-only harness) and report the exit time.

Deliverable: `doc/plan/c016-worklog/fix-dotnet-session-reject-blocking-send-summary.md`. Do not print it.
